## Runner corrections and owner decisions (SDD-007)

All corrections are host configuration in `evals/` and `scripts/native-probes/`; no product change.

- Allowed tools aligned with SDD-007. Owner decision 2026-10-16: `with_skills` = AGDF MCP tools, `Skill`, `Read`, `Bash` and `PowerShell` (Claude Code's shell on Windows); `mcp_only` = AGDF MCP tools and `Read`.
- `--tools` limits the built-in tool set, because `--allowedTools` does not restrict tools. Owner decision 2026-10-16: `ToolSearch` stays in both variants so that Claude Code loads MCP tools on demand as in normal use.
- claude.ai connectors are disabled for the isolated home (`ENABLE_CLAUDEAI_MCP_SERVERS=false`). Discovery stops before the first paid session if any other MCP server is present.
- A free MCP check (`claude mcp list`) runs before each session, with one retry after 30 s. A cell whose check fails is `aborted` with `mcp_unavailable` and launcher diagnostics, at no cost.
- Variant verification additionally rejects other MCP servers and built-in tools outside the variant.
- Cleaned per-session transcripts are written to gitignored `probe-results` for checking the predicates and are never promoted. Cleaning covers local roots in every escaping depth, Git Bash and Claude project-directory forms, the user name, the git identity and non-AGDF server names.

## Observations for the later phases

- Success, run 3 (with_skills / mcp_only, 4 sessions each): T1 0/4 vs 4/4, T2 4/4 vs 0/4, T3 4/4 vs 1/4, T4 0/4 vs 0/4, T5 2/4 vs 0/4, T6 4/4 vs 4/4.
- T2 `mcp_only`: the intake can only continue through the CLI `run-create`, and no MCP tool creates a run. MCP-only agents cannot start a delivery run.
- T4: no session completed `agdf_inspect` `presentation-document`; every attempt failed SDK validation on required fields the schema does not describe (F04).
- T5: the failures are `target_unresolved` because `target_source` was omitted (F03, F05).
- T1 `with_skills`: the agents read the control files through the shell instead of calling AGDF.
- T6 passes when the agent writes nothing; the transcripts show that the agents recognized the stale revision and asked. This limitation is stated in `REPORT.md`.
- The run 2 connect timeouts are unexplained; the isolated home was already removed and no processes remained. The pre-session check now records launcher diagnostics if they recur (F09).

